\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{The alternating form of a kernel}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{Let #{E} be finite free of even rank #{2s} over a
commutative ring #{k}, with a perfect alternating bilinear
form #{B}. For #{K\in\operatorname{End}_k(E)}, its
\newvocab{kernel form} relative to #{B} is
##{A_{B,K}(x,y)=B(x,Ky).}
The condition that this form be alternating is
#{B(x,Kx)=0} for every #{x\in E}. Its
\vocabk{ring Pfaffian}{fdip-00UR} is used only when this
alternation condition holds.}
